  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/635e7d6b-f51c-41dc-8493-fafd5eb8c158-image.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 98px;\" /></p><p>Aldehydic (-CHO)&nbsp;group has greater priority than keto&nbsp;group and nitro groups is always a prefix.</p><p>Root word of the given compound is hept, double bond is the primary suffix and aldehydic group becomes secondary suffix and keto and nitro groups are prefixes.</p><p>Hence, the correct IUPAC name of the given compound is</p><p>4-Methyl-6-nitro-3-oxohept-4-enal</p>",
    "image": null
  },
